patrone-branding (0.1.23) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The system is PatroneOS, as the user named it on 2026-10-29: os-release
    (NAME, PRETTY_NAME, and HOME_URL https://patroneos.com), lsb-release,
    the boot menu (GRUB takes os-release's NAME), the text boot screen,
    /etc/issue, /etc/legal, the cursor theme's description and this
    package's description. The links to the code and its issues go to the
    repository's new name, github.com/billsecond/patroneos. Nothing here
    says the old name any more, earlier entries of this changelog included
    (the user: "remove anything that says" it).
  * The PatroneOS logo, from the user's Neon Horizon pictures: the P beside
    or over a PATRONEOS wordmark, OS in Patrone Blue, in place of the first
    logo's wordmark. It's drawn as vector shapes in code
    (tools/patrone_logo.py), and every logo file is drawn from them:
    Settings > About, the login screen, the boot splash, the installer's and
    first-login setup's pictures, the logo icons and fastfetch's logo. The
    SVG masters are installed in /usr/share/patrone/logos. Patrone's colors
    are unchanged.
  * The Neon Horizon wallpaper (02), enlarged to 7680x4320 with its logo
    drawn again sharp, is the default in both styles and on the lock
    screen, with a family like wallpaper 01's (light, no logo, mark, clean,
    badge, midnight, blue, graphite, watermark), and wallpaper 03 from the
    user's other picture. Wallpaper 01's family is retired; its file names
    are links to 02's, so a desktop set to one keeps a wallpaper.
  * The copyright file records that both pictures were made with ChatGPT
    (their C2PA manifests, signed by OpenAI).

