patrone-branding (0.1.20) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Patrone's own cursors in place of Ubuntu's (the user saw Ubuntu's busy
    cursor while something loaded): every cursor in Patrone's blues with a
    white edge, and the busy cursors with the boot splash's spinner, a
    comet running round a ring. tools/make_cursors.py draws them at build
    time, at 24 to 96 pixels for HiDPI screens, with links for the names
    X11, Qt, Chromium and Yaru use; Adwaita's stand in for any missing.
    They're the default for the desktop, apps and the login screen, and
    the system's default cursor theme (x-cursor-theme) for everything else.

