    Patrone's P (tools/make_logo_icons.sh; Yaru's are moved aside), in every
    color of Yaru's icons and its dark style. os-release's LOGO,
    patrone-logo, is in the hicolor theme too, for programs that look only
    in icon themes.
  * /etc/legal says where the list of what the system connects to is.
  * The copyright file says how the logo and wallpaper 01 were made: with
    an AI image generator (OpenAI's ChatGPT, as the wallpaper's signed C2PA
    manifest records), so they're offered under GPL-3+ only as far as
    anyone holds copyright in them (docs/COMPLIANCE.md, item 9).
  * The installer's settings no longer list the pages of "Automated with
    Landscape", Canonical's management service, whose choice
    patrone-installer 0.1.4 takes out.

